Using the LDDRK time-integration scheme can reduce temporal dispersion. However, achieving a comparable level of accuracy requires a computational 
cost similar to, or even slightly higher than, that of the Newmark scheme with a smaller time step. In addition, LDDRK produces relatively large 
errors for weak back-scattered and reflected waves, which cannot reduced with refined mesh. This issue may arise from the mismatch between the 
wavefield and the corresponding time representation (i.e., the wavefield is evaluated at Δt × (istep -1 +fraction)
